{
  "behaviour": "lfm/1",
  "kind": "render",
  "description": "Heading ids, slugs and deduplication (sec. 4.6), anchors (sec. 12), ToC (sec. 10.6). render(text, media, profile) vectors (docs/spec/lfm-1.md). input: {text | gen, media?, profile?, encoding_error?}; gen = prefix + repeat*times + suffix. expected holds only the asserted Rendered fields (html, styled, text, excerpt, toc, word_count, read_minutes, links, mentions, media_used, anchors, flags, error) plus derived fields: html_temml (Temml-mode HTML, sec. 7.5), text_x (P_x, sec. 10.3), html_head/html_tail (first/last 400 chars of html), html_rle (html lines, runs of identical lines as 'line \u00d7N'), html_bytes (UTF-8 length of html). Every render vector is also checked against the sec. 13 invariants (allowlist, idempotence, sanitiser equality, terminal escapes). Inputs generated by lfm1/gen_inputs.py; expected values blessed with LESSDUGIN_BLESS=1 and reviewed.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "basic-slug",
      "input": {
        "text": "# Hello, World!\n"
      },
      "expected": {
        "html": "<div class=\"lfm\" dir=\"auto\">\n<h1 id=\"md-h-hello-world\" dir=\"auto\">Hello, World!</h1>\n</div>\n",
        "anchors": [
          "md-h-hello-world"
        ],
        "toc": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "id": "md-h-hello-world",
            "text": "Hello, World!"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
